====Verb====
[[Image:Cincinnati-life-insurance-building-detail.jpg|thumb|fluted [[pillar]]s]]
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To play on a [[#Noun|flute]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a [[flutelike]] sound.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1895|author=S. R. Crockett|title=A Cry Across the Black Water
|passage=The green turf was velvet underfoot. The blackbirds '''fluted''' in the hazels there.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To utter with a [[flutelike]] sound.
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XIII|passage=“Oh, there's my precious Poppet,” said Phyllis, as a distant barking reached the ears. “He's asking for his dinner, the sweet little angel. All right, darling, Mother's coming,” she '''fluted''', and buzzed off on the errand of mercy.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To form flutes or channels in (as in a column, a ruffle, etc.); to cut a semicylindrical vertical groove in (as in a pillar, etc.).

