====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lbl|en|intransitive}} To put forth [[bloom]]s.
#: {{ux|en|This plant '''flowers''' in June.}}
# {{lbl|en|transitive}} To decorate with pictures of flowers.
# {{lbl|en|intransitive}} To reach a state of full [[development]] or achievement.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Shepheardes Calender|December|year=1586|text=when '''flowr'd''' my youthful spring}}
#* '''1940''' {{w|Mahadev Desai}}, translator, {{w|Mahatma Gandhi}}, ''An Autobiography'', Part III (IX) The Story of My Experiments with Truth/Part III/Simple Life, original published 1927-1929
#*: It only needed watering to take root, to '''flower''' and to fructify, and the watering came in due course.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Naomi Wolf|title=Vagina: A New Biography|page=43
|passage=In life after life of this now-expanded circle of women artists, writers and revolutionaries, the same appeared: a flowing of creative insight and vision seemed the follow a sexual '''flowering'''.}}
# {{lbl|en|archaic|intransitive}} To froth; to ferment gently, as new beer.
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=That beer did '''flower''' a little.}}
# {{lbl|en|intransitive}} To come off as flowers by [[sublimation]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Of Education|passage=observations which have '''flowered''' off}}

