# {{senseid|en|buoyant}} A [[buoyant]] [[device]] used to [[support]] something in [[water]] or another [[liquid]].
#: {{ux|en|Attach the '''float''' and the weight to the fishing line, above the hook.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|title=The Fisherman Who Laughed|page=40|passage='What you need are frogs,' said the veteran. 'Fish them at night. There's nothing like them on big cork '''floats'''.'}}
# A [[mass]] of [[timber]] or [[board]]s [[fasten]]ed [[together]], and [[convey]]ed [[down]] a [[stream]] by the [[current]]; a [[raft]].
# A [[float board]].
# A [[tool]] similar to a [[rasp]], used in various [[trade]]s.
# A sort of [[trowel]] used for [[finish]]ing [[concrete]] [[surface]]s or [[smooth]]ing [[plaster]].
#: {{ux|en|When pouring a new driveway, you can use a two-by-four as a '''float'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|parade}} An [[elaborate]]ly [[decorated]] [[trailer]] or [[vehicle]], [[intended]] for [[display]] in a [[parade]] or [[pageant]].
#: {{ux|en|That '''float''' covered in roses is very pretty.}}
# A floating [[toy]] made of [[foam]], used in [[swimming pool]]s.
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[small]] [[vehicle]] used for [[local]] [[delivery|deliveries]], especially in the term {{m|en|milk float}}.
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Sons and Lovers|passage=As soon as the skies brightened and plum-blossom was out, Paul drove off in the milkman's heavy '''float''' up to Willey Farm.|7}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} [[funds|Funds]] [[committed]] to be [[paid]] but not yet paid.
#: {{ux|en|Our bank does a nightly sweep of accounts, to adjust the '''float''' so we stay within our reserves limit.}}
# {{lb|en|finance|Australia|and other Commonwealth countries?}} An [[offering]] of [[share]]s in a [[company]] (or [[unit]]s in a [[trust]]) to [[member]]s of the [[public]], normally [[followed]] by a [[listing]] on a [[stock exchange]].
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2006|passage=You don't actually need a broker to buy shares in a '''float''' when a company is about to be listed on the Australian Stock Exchange.|work=[[w:Australian Securities and Investments Commission|Australian Securities and Investments Commission]] financial tips article|title=Buying shares in a float|url=http://www.fido.asic.gov.au/fido/fido.nsf/print/Buying+shares+in+a+float?opendocument|accessdate=2 March 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20050716011533/http://www.fido.asic.gov.au/fido/fido.nsf/print/Buying+shares+in+a+float?opendocument|archivedate=16 July 2005}}
# {{lb|en|banking}} The [[total]] [[amount]] of [[check]]s/[[cheque]]s or other [[draft]]s [[write|written]] against a [[bank account]] but not yet [[clear]]ed and [[charge]]d against the account.
#: {{ux|en|No sir, your current '''float''' is not taken into account, when assets are legally garnished.}}
# {{lb|en|insurance}} [[premium|Premium]]s [[take in|taken in]] but not yet [[pay out|paid out]].
#: {{ux|en|We make a lot of interest from our nightly '''float'''.}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} A [[floating-point number]], especially one that has lower [[precision]] than a [[double]].
#: {{ux|en|That routine should not have used an int; it should be a '''float'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Rubin H. Landau|title=A First Course in Scientific Computing|page=214
|passage=If you want to be a scientist or an engineer, learn to say “no” to singles and '''floats'''.}}
# A [[soft]] [[beverage]] with a [[scoop]] of [[ice cream]] [[#Verb|float]]ing in it.
#: {{ux|en|I don't consider anything other than root-beer with vanilla ice cream to be a "real" '''float'''.}}
# A [[small]] [[sum]] of [[money]] put in a [[cashier]]'s [[till]], or otherwise [[secure]]d, at the [[start]] of [[business]], to [[enable]] [[change]] to be made.
# {{lb|en|poker}} A [[maneuver]] where a [[player]] [[call]]s on the [[flop]] or [[turn]] with a [[weak]] [[hand]], with the [[intention]] of [[bluff#Verb|bluffing]] after a subsequent [[community card]].
# {{lb|en|weaving}} A [[weft]] thread that passes over two or more [[warp]] threads (or less commonly, warp over weft).
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Handweaver's Notebook|author=Sharon Alderman|year=1990|ISBN=0934026572|page=82|text=I knew that a simple '''float''' on the surface of the Merino might catch if I made it big enough to show very much.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Weaver's Book of 8-Shaft Patterns|editor=Carol Strickler|year=1991|publisher=Interweave Press|ISBN=093402667X|page=140-141
|text=The appearance of a waffle fabric changes drastically with washing. Yarns differ, but most relax and twist and curl in the long '''floats''' when washed; the severe rectilinear design of the waffle cells in unwashed waffle weave fabric will soften dramatically.}}
# {{lb|en|knitting}} A loose strand of yarn that passes behind one or more stitches when knitting with multiple yarns.
# {{lb|en|basketry}} A [[decorative]] [[rod]] that extends over the body of a [[basket]] without being attached for part of its length.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Rachel Nash Law; Cynthia Wieboldt Taylor|title=Appalachian White Oak Basketmaking: Handing Down the Basket|page=xii
|passage=Rod Basket with Serpentine '''Floats'''}}
# {{lb|en|automotive}} A [[car carrier]] or [[car transporter]] [[truck]] or truck-and-[[trailer]] combination.
# {{lb|en|transport}} A [[lowboy]] [[trailer]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of [[flow]]ing; [[flux]]; [[flow]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Henry 7|passage=Hee being now in '''Float''' for Treasure.}}
# A [[polishing]] [[block]] used in [[marble]] [[working]]; a [[runner]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 24, 1863|work=The Building News and Engineering Journal |title=Trade News|author=|volume=10|page=324|passage=The machinery consists of two saws, a polishing table, a '''float''' for grinding marble, and a ripping saw for cutting slabs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1925| title=Commonwealth Arbitration Reports|author=Australia. Commonwealth Court of Conciliation and Arbitration | page=557| passage=''Float Machinist''— One who squares up, faces, noses or chamfers on a '''float''' all marble, slate, or similar stones, and including terrazzo or similar compositions.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980| title=Bulletin of the United States Bureau of Labor Statistics|author=| page=215| passage=Next , finishers rub a '''float''' — a small and smooth, rectangular piece of wood — over the entire surface, carefully avoiding edges and joints.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015| title=Materials for Construction and Civil Engineering|author=M. Clara Gonçalves; Fernanda Margarido | page=102| passage=Floated: Obtained by successive passages with a wooden '''float''' on the coat's surface until it is flat and uniform }}
# {{lb|en|UK|dated}} A [[coal]] [[cart]].<ref>{{R:Simmonds Trade}}</ref>
# A [[breakdancing]] [[move]] in which the body is held [[parallel]] to the [[floor]] while [[balance|balancing]] on one or both [[hand]]s.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[visual]] [[style]] on a [[web page]] that causes the styled [[element]]s to [[#Verb|float]] [[above]] or [[beside]] others.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Eric A. Meyer|title=More Eric Meyer on CSS|page=36
|passage=Because margin '''floats''' don't collapse together, the actual spacing between two '''floats''' sitting next to each other will be 6 pixels {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=Michael Bowers|title=Pro CSS and HTML Design Patterns|page=93
|passage=When a '''float''' cannot fit next to another float, it moves down below it. A float's position, size, padding, borders, and margins affect the position of adjacent floats and adjacent inline content.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} The [[gas]]-[[filled]] [[sac]], [[bag]]{{,}} or [[body]] of a [[siphonophore]]; a [[pneumatophore]].
# {{senseid|en|document element}} {{lb|en|publishing|digital typesetting}} Any object (element) whose location in composition (page makeup, pagination) does not flow within {{l|en|body text}} but rather floats outside of it, usually anchored loosely (in {{l|en|buoy}} metaphor) to spots within it (citations, callouts): a figure (image), table, box, pull quote, ornament, or other {{l|en|float|id=place a document element|floated}} element.

