===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q217164}}{{lb|en|countable}} The interior bottom or surface of a house or building; the supporting surface of a room.
#: {{ux|en|The room has a wooden '''floor'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Belloc Lowndes Lodger|I|0016
|passage=A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the '''floor'''; as, again, the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire.}}
# {{lb|en|geology|biology|chiefly with a modifier}} The bottom surface of a natural structure, entity, or space {{gl|e.g. cave, forest, ocean, desert, etc.}}; the [[ground]] {{gl|surface of the Earth}}.
#: {{ux|en|The leaves covering the forest '''floor''' provide many hiding-places for small animals.}}
#: {{ux|en|Many sunken ships rest on the ocean '''floor'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''floor''' of a cave served the refugees as a home.}}
#: {{ux|en|The pit '''floor''' showed where a ring of post holes had been.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1989|month=May|volume=175|number=5|title=Venezuela's Islands in Time|author=Uwe George|page=561
|text=The '''floor''' of the cave was covered with white sand that had been washed in by the river.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|dialectal|colloquial}} The [[ground]].
#: {{usex|en|After stepping off the bus, my wallet fell on the '''floor'''.}}
# {{lb|en|construction|architecture}} A structure formed of beams, girders, etc, with proper covering, which divides a building horizontally into [[storey]]s/[[story|stories]].
# The supporting surface or platform of a structure such as a bridge.
#: {{ux|en|Wooden planks of the old bridge's '''floor''' were nearly rotten.}}
# {{sid|en|Q831691}}{{lb|en|architecture|countable}} A [[storey]]/[[story]] of a building.
#: {{ux|en|For years we lived on the third '''floor'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=19|passage=When Timothy and Julia hurried up the staircase to the bedroom '''floor''', where a considerable commotion was taking place, Tim took Barry Leach with him. He had him gripped firmly by the arm, since he felt it was not safe to let him loose, and he had no immediate idea what to do with him.}}
# In a [[parliament]], the part of the house assigned to the members, as opposed to the viewing gallery.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The right to speak at a given time during a debate or other public event.
#: {{ux|en|Will the senator from Arizona yield the '''floor'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|The mayor often gives a lobbyist the '''floor'''.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} That part of the bottom of a vessel on each side of the keelson which is most nearly horizontal.
# {{lb|en|mining}} A horizontal, flat ore body; the rock underlying a stratified or nearly horizontal deposit.
# {{lb|en|mining}} The bottom of a pit, pothole or mine.<ref>{{R:Raymond Glossary}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The largest [[integer]] less than or equal to a given number.
#: {{ux|en|The '''floor''' of 4.5 is 4.}}
# {{lb|en|gymnastics}} An [[event]] performed on a floor-like carpeted surface; [[floor exercise]]
# {{lb|en|gymnastics}} A floor-like carpeted surface for performing gymnastic movements.
# {{lb|en|finance}} A lower limit or minimum on a price or rate, a [[price floor]]. Opposite of a [[cap]] or [[ceiling]].
# A [[dance floor]].
#* '''1983''', "[[w:Maniac (song)|Maniac]]", Michael Sembello and Dennis Matkosky:
#*: She's a maniac, maniac on the '''floor''' / And she's dancing like she never danced before
#* '''1987''', "{{w|Walk the Dinosaur}}", {{w|Was (Not Was)}}:
#*: Open the door, get on the '''floor''' / Everybody walk the dinosaur
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Ed Sheeran;w:Ilya Salmanzadeh;w:Johnny McDaid;w:Savan Kotecha|authorlabel=no|title=w:[[Azizam (song)|Azizam]]|album=w:[[Play (Ed Sheeran album)|Play]]|date=4 April 2025|artist=Ed Sheeran|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PeuA_714KQg|text=Meet me on the '''floor''' tonight<br>Show me how to move like the water}}
# The [[trading floor]] of a [[stock exchange]], [[pit]]; the area in which business is conducted at a [[convention]] or [[exhibition]].
# The area of a [[casino]] where [[gambling]] occurs.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Tim Hatton|title=Tock Tock Birds: A Spider in the Web of International Terrorism|url= https://www.google.com/books/edition/Tock_Tock_Birds/CpqfAAAAMAAJ?kptab=editions&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiyw8yN9Mn7AhUGZcAKHdEeAm44FBCYFnoECAUQBw|page=284|passage=At each table stood a young, slim, poker-faced croupier serving the punters who anxiously watched the turning of the cards. The next two '''floors''' were similar though not quite as spectacular and the stakes were lower.}}
# The area of an establishment where food and drink are served to customers.
#* {{quote-book|en|date=1947-03-18|author=U.S. Government Printing Office|title=Proceedings and Debates of the Congress, Eightieth Congress, First Session|page=2206|pageurl= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Congressional_Record/1dZ9ycwelJwC?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=waitress%7Cwaitresses+serve%7Cserves%7Cserved+the+floor&pg=PA2206&printsec=frontcover |passage=The conference started as an impromptu session in the coffee shop this morning when waitresses walked off the '''floor''' rather than serve four Negro men and women delegates.}}

