===Etymology===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = Blue Sky Of Bangladesh.jpg
|caption1 = The firmament ''(sense 1)'' or [[sky]].
|image2 = Ptolemaicsystem-small.png
|caption2 = One version of the [[Ptolemaic]] [[system]] of [[celestial sphere]]s, with the firmament (indicated in Latin as ''Firmamentu''[''m'']; ''sense 3'') shown as the eighth [[heaven#Noun|heaven]]{{ref|group=n|name=n1|From {{cite-book|author=Petrus Apianus|authorlink=Petrus Apianus|author2=Gemma Frisius|authorlink2=Gemma Frisius|title=Petri Apiani cosmographia, per Gemmam Phrysium, apud Louanienses medicum ac mathematicum insignem, restituta: additis de adem re ipsius Gemmae Phry. libellis, ut sequens pagina docet|location=Antwerp|publisher=In pingui gallina Arnoldo Berckma[n]no [Arnold Birckmann]|year=1539|oclc=1113627241}}.}}
}}

{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰer-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|firmament}}, {{m|enm|furmament|t=heaven; sky}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|pos=n|id=MED16055}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|firmament|t=firmament}}, or from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|firmāmentum|t=support; sky}}, from
{{m|la|firmāre|t=to strengthen}} + {{m|la|-mentum|pos=suffix indicating an instrument or medium, or the result of an action}}. ''Firmāre'' is the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|firmō|t=to make firm, strengthen}}, from {{m|la|firmus|t=firm, strong, stable}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰer-|t=to hold; to support}}.<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=70586|date=1896|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

The Latin word was used in the {{w|Vulgate}} version of the [[Bible]] to translate the
{{noncog|grc|στερέωμα|t=foundation, framework; firmament}} in the {{w|Septuagint}} (Greek [[Old Testament]]), which in turn was used to translate the {{noncog|he|רָקִיעַ|tr=rāqī́aʿ|t=celestial dome, vault of heaven}}, from the root {{m|he|ר־ק־ע|tr=r-q-`}}; in [[w:Syriac language|Classical Syriac]] the similar root {{syc-root|ܪ ܩ ܥ}} (related to compacting) gave rise to {{m|syc|ܪܩܝܥܐ|tr=rəqīʿā|t=compact; firm; firmament, heavens, sky; celestial sphere}}.<ref name="OED"/>

